      "proof": "On the lift index k, the next-step numerator divided by two is an affine map with odd coefficient modulo 2^B, hence a permutation. Exactly 2^(B-b) residues have next valuation b for 1<=b<=B, while one residue has valuation greater than B. Multiplying child masses proves the word law. The number of positive compositions of s into m parts is binom(s-1,m-1), which gives the negative-binomial formula. Applying Markov's inequality to exp(-t sum a_i) and optimizing t gives the reported Chernoff base.",
